 conclusion hoga, aur (c) kaunsa observed pattern falsify karega ki \"clipping error vs round-off error tradeoff\" hi dominant mechanism hai. Ye three-way outcome interpretation main deliverable ka sabse important hissa hai.\n\n6) Controls: fp16 anchor, alpha=1.0 round-off-only check, aur deterministic eval — teen theek hain. Ek aur add kijiye: ek trivial-quantization control (e.g., deliberately over-clipped alpha jaise 0.3) jo verify kare ki harness clipping sensitivity detect kar sakta hai aur PPL response meaningful direction me hai.\n\n7) Feasibility: analytical CPU estimate rakhiye, smoke-test-derived throughput ko hypothetical maankar; koi bhi number \"measured\" label ke saath na aaye, jab tak aapne sach me command na chalaya ho. Reduced-token fallback budget explicitly dijiye.\n\nKoi result ya empirical claim mat dijiye — deliverable rationale, configs, procedure, controls, analysis plan aur feasibility tak seemit rahe.", "required_handoff_stage": "result", "approach_approved": true}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
