Let me construct the complete design. Some computational estimates are analytical: e.g., FLOPs per token ~2*params = 14 GFLOP/token forward pass (7B params → ~13.2B non-embedding params, 2*13.2 ≈ 26 GFLOPs forward... actually forward pass FLOPs ≈ 2 * params * tokens = 2*6.7e9 = 13.4 GFLOPs/token for the forward pass). CPU throughput per core probably 10–50 GFLOPS (AVX2); with 224 cores at decent parallel scaling, probably 1–5 TFLOPS achievable → 100–400 tokens/s hypothetically. Keep it as an analytical range with clear "analytical, not measured" labels.

Eval budget: WikiText-2 test ~250k tokens, 2048-token segments → ~122 segments. Full: 10 configs × 250k tokens = 2.5M tokens. At an analytical 50–300 tok/s → 2.3–14 hours. Fallback: 512 segments... wait no, WikiText-2 test only gives ~122 segments of 2048. Fallback: 64 segments (~131k tokens) per config. Let me do the math: raw wikitext-2 test ~245k tokens → /2048 ≈ 120 segments. Reduced-budget fallback: 32 segments per config (~65k tokens) → 10 configs = 655k tokens.

Design structure:

1. Objective and fixed requirements (verbatim): LLAMA2-7B; input activation path symmetric; KV cache path asymmetric; metric = perplexity.
2. Named assumption A1: clipping definition θ = α·absmax (α ≤ 1), applied per-quantization-unit (per-token for activations; per-group for K, per-channel for V). Include a definition-mapping note:
   - Percentile-based: α_p ∈ {70,75,...,100} percentile of |x| within the quantization unit; mapping: the α values are the same numbers but interpreted as percentiles; at α=100 percentile ≈ absmax (≈ our α=1.0).
   - Absmax multiplier >1: θ = β·absmax, β ≥ 1; grid β ∈ {1.00, 1.02, 1.05,... } hmm, remapping our 7-point grid: β = 1/α → {1.43, 1.33, 1.25, 1.18, 1.11, 1.05, 1.00}. Note that under this definition clipping means... actually a multiplier >1 means no clipping (superset) and larger β increases the quantization step. So the tradeoff mechanism is inverted: β=1 is minimal step. Mapping note: our α=1.0 ↔ β=1.0; our α grid maps to β = 1/α ∈ {1.43,...,1.05}. Note that the "clipping never helps" regime corresponds to β>1 where increasing β monotonically worsens rounding — this definition has no clipping benefit at all... actually, a multiplier >1 gives no clipping at all and just expands the step, so it monotonically degrades; still, the mapping note suffices.
3. Models and software: Llama-2-7B-hf fp16; transformers + torch; runtime quantization hooks: activation quantization applied to input activations of attention/FFN (specify the target: input of each linear layer) symmetric per-token A8; KV cache asymmetric 4-bit, per-token-group K group=32, per-channel V.
4. Grid: primary α grid, 7 points {0.70,0.75,0.80,0.85,0.90,0.95,1.00}; shared α. Plus control α=0.30. Plus refinement: quadratic interpolation around argmin.
