 and run-time arithmetic, not the protocol)"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-2f7389a4-3d47-4d2a-be07-7508dd54102d", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "end_researcher_turn: {"stage": "result", "answer": "# Experiment Design: Effect of Fixed Clipping Ratio on Perplexity of LLAMA2-7B under Symmetric Input-Activation and Asymmetric KV-Cache Runtime Quantization\n\n**Deliverable type:** design only. No experiment was run; every quantitative figure below is an analytical estimate or a design parameter, never a measurement.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Fixed requirements (honored verbatim, no ambiguity permitted)\n\n- **Model:** LLAMA2-7B (Meta Llama-2 7B, HuggingFace fp16 weights; weights themselves remain unquantized).\n- **Input-activation path:** **symmetric** uniform quantization (zero-point = 0), applied at runtime.\n- **KV-cache path:** **asymmetric** uniform quantization (min\u2013max with zero-point), applied at runtime when writing K and V to the cache.\n- **Metric:** **perplexity** (next-token cross-entropy, exp-averaged).\n- **Headline question:** one **shared, fixed** clipping ratio \u03b1 across input and KV paths (the question asks for \"the optimal fixed clipping ratio\", singular). Independent per-path ratios appear only in an optional ablation tier (\u00a77).\n\n## 2. Named assumption A1 \u2014 clipping-ratio definition (primary, anchored)\n\n**A1 (assumption, not a source-confirmed fact):** the clip threshold is\n**\u03b8 = \u03b1 \u00b7 absmax(tensor-unit)**, with **\u03b1 \u2264 1**, computed per quantization unit (per token for activations; per group/channel for KV; \u00a73). Swept grid: **\u03b1 \u2208 {0.70, 0.75, 0.80, 0.85, 0.90, 0.95, 1.00}**. Rationale: \u03b1=1.0 is the no-clipping round-off-only endpoint; \u03b1<~0.8 is the clipping-distortion-dominated regime; 7 points bracket and resolve the expected interior trade-off, with parabolic refinement (\u00a76a).\n\n**Definition-mapping note** (if the source paper defines \u03b1 differently, the same 7-point structure remaps as follows; headline answer remains anchored to A1 unless the source pins another definition):\n- *Percentile-based:* \u03b8 = quantile_{p}(|x|) within the unit; use **p \u2208 {70, 75, 80, 85, 90, 95, 100}** \u2014 same seven numbers, reinterpreted as percentiles; p=100 \u2248 absmax plays the role of A1's \u03b1=1.0.\n- *Absmax multiplier >1:* \u03b8 = \u03b2\u00b7absmax with \u03b2 \u2265 1 (over-range instead of clipping); map via **\u03b2 = 1/\u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 \u2208 {1.43, 1.33, 1.25, 1.18, 1.11, 1.05, 1.00}**. Note the mechanism inverts in direction: \u03b2>1 only inflates the quantization step (no clipping benefit), so a monotone-decreasing ppl in \u03b2 with optimum at \u03b2=1.0 is the expected shape; an interior minimum in \u03b2 would indicate robustness to step size rather than a clipping trade-off.\n\n## 3. Quantization configuration (design parameters, not brief-fixed \u2014 see sensitivity tier \u00a77)\n\n- **Activations (symmetric, per-token):** 8 bit (A8), per-token granularity: \u03b8 recomputed per token from that token's absmax \u00d7 \u03b1. Applied to input activations of the linear layers (attention QKV/O inputs and MLP up/gate/down inputs).\n- **KV cache (asymmetric):** 4 bit (K4-V4); **K quantized per token-group (group size 32)**, **V quantized per channel** (head-dim channel, across cached tokens); \u03b8_K, \u03b8_V from min\u2013max within each group/channel scaled by \u03b1 (under A1, asymmetric scaling means widening: [min \u2212 (\u03b1\u22121)\u00b7range\u2026] is not applicable for \u03b1\u22641, so \u03b1<1 contracts the stored range and clips extremes on both ends; the clipping interpretation of \u03b1 is identical in spirit for the asymmetric path).\n- **Context/protocol:** 2048-token contiguous segments, causal LM scoring, no sliding window, per-token equal weighting.\n- **No calibration data is required under A1** (\u03b1 is fixed a priori \u2014 that is the point of \"fixed clipping ratio\"). Only the percentile variant would need a calibration subset (WikiText-2 train, 128\u00d72048) to estimate percentiles.\n\n## 4. Data\n\n- **Primary eval:** WikiText-2 test split (\u22480.24\u20130.25 M tokens \u2248 ~119 segments of 2048; exact count to be verified at implementation), standard Llama-2 tokenization.\n- **Secondary eval (robustness of the selected \u03b1\\* only):** PTB test, run at \u03b1\\*, \u03b1=1.0 and \u03b1=0.30 (4 points max).\n\n## 5. Runs (configs table)\n\n| ID | Purpose | \u03b1 (shared) | Bits / granularity | Corpus |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| C0 | fp16 anchor (quantization off) | \u2014 | fp16 | WikiText-2 |\n| C1\u2013C7 | **primary sweep** | 0.70 / 0.75 / 0.80 / 0.85 / 0.90 / 0.95 / 1.00 | A8 per-token sym; K4-V4 asym (g=32 / per-ch) | WikiText-2 |\n| C8 | trivial-quantization control | 0.30 | same as C1\u2013C7 | WikiText-2 |\n| C9\u2013C11 | secondary-corpus check | \u03b1\\*, 1.00, 0.30 | same | PTB |\n| **Optional tier A** (shared-\u03b1 confirmation) | 3\u00d73 (\u03b1_input \u00d7 \u03b1_kv) subgrid | {0.8, 0.9, 1.0}\u00b2 | same | WikiText-2, reduced tokens |\n| **Sensitivity tier B** (\u22643 extra points, not a factorial) | see \u00a77 | \u03b1\\* (+1.0) | see \u00a77 | WikiText-2, reduced tokens |\n\nTotal main experiment: 12 WikiText-2 runs + 3 PTB runs (optional tiers add at most 9 + 3\u20134 cheap runs).\n\n## 6. Analysis plan (primary deliverable)\n\n**(a) argmin + plateau reporting.** Report the ppl(\u03b1) curve for C1\u2013C7 against the C0 fp16 anchor; **\u03b1\\* = argmin ppl(\u03b1)**. Report the **robust plateau band** = {\u03b1 : ppl(\u03b1) \u2264 1.01 \u00b7 ppl(\u03b1\\*)} as the practical recommendation (a range, with \u03b1\\* as the point estimate). Sub-grid estimate: fit a quadratic to the three points bracketing \u03b1\\* (only if \u03b1\\* is interior) and report the vertex. Deterministic eval \u21d2 single run per config, no seeds/variance estimation needed; if any nondeterminism (thread-count reduction kernels) is detected, add one repeat at \u03b1\\* and report the spread.\n\n**(b) Monotone boundary optimum (optimum at \u03b1=1.0).** If ppl(\u03b1) is monotone decreasing toward \u03b1=1.0, conclude: **under definition A1 at A8/K4-V4, clipping never helps on this model/corpus; the optimal fixed clipping ratio is \u03b1=1.0 (i.e., absmax, round-off only)**, and the headline trade-off claim is negative for this regime. Supporting diagnostics distinguish \"genuinely round-off-dominated\" (activation/KV MSE and logit-KL grow monotonically as \u03b1 decreases; the \u03b1=1.0 run matches the analytical round-off expectation \u2014 \u00a78) from \"grid mis-specified\" (curve still steeply decreasing at \u03b1=0.70 \u21d2 extend the grid one decade lower before concluding).\n\n**(c) Falsification of the clipping-vs-round-off trade-off as dominant mechanism.** Expected signature of the trade-off is a unimodal (U-shaped) curve with interior minimum. Patterns that would **falsify** trade-off dominance:\n1. **Non-unimodal curve** (multiple local minima or step discontinuities at specific \u03b1) \u21d2 behavior is driven by outlier tokens flipping per-token absmax and by group-boundary effects, not by a smooth two-error trade-off.\n2. **Flat response** \u2014 ppl variation across the grid within harness noise (< ~0.1% relative) while activation/KV MSE demonstrably grows with clipping \u21d2 quantization error is not propagating to the loss; downstream robustness, not error minimization, sets ppl, so no meaningful \u03b1\\* exists at these bit-widths.\n3. **Metric dissociation** \u2014 \u03b1-MSE/KL minima and the ppl minimum disagree materially (e.g., KL minimized at 0.90 but ppl pinned at 1.0, or vice versa) with the gap exceeding run-to-run harness noise \u21d2 the loss-vs-\u03b1 mapping is not monotone in quantization error and the simple trade-off model does not predict the observed optimum.\n   Additionally, if the \u03b1=0.30 control does **not** produce a large, clearly ordered ppl degradation (\u00a78, C8), the harness \u2014 not the mechanism \u2014 is in question and no outcome (b)-type conclusion may be drawn.\n\n**Secondary metrics (per config):** (i) MSE between quantized and fp16 activation and K/V tensors (sampled layers); (ii) mean per-token KL of next-token logits vs. C0; (iii) peak memory and tokens/sec (reported as runtime observations when executed; here only as planned instrumentation).\n\n## 7. Sensitivity note (bit-width/granularity; \u22643 extra points, explicitly not a factorial)\n\n\u03b1\\* is a design parameter chosen jointly with bit-widths/granularity; whether it shifts is checked cheaply:\n- **S1 (bit-width shift):** rerun \u03b1 \u2208 {\u03b1\\*, 1.00} at **K8-V8** (2 points). If the (\u03b1\\*,1.0) ppl gap collapses at 8 bit, the optimum is expected to migrate toward 1.0 (round-off dominates at higher precision); if the gap persists, the optimum is bit-width-robust.\n- **S2 (granularity shift):** rerun \u03b1 = \u03b1\\* with **per-tensor symmetric** activations (1 point). A materially different ppl at the same \u03b1 indicates the optimum depends on granularity (per-token absmax tracks outliers better than per-tensor).\n- **S3 (optional, low-bit stress):** \u03b1 = \u03b1\\* at K2-V2 (1 point), testing whether the optimum moves downward at aggressive KV precision, where clipping outliers matters most.\nEach point is a single reduced-token run; conclusion reported as direction + approximate magnitude of the shift, not as a swept surface.\n\n## 8. Controls\n\n1. **C0 fp16 anchor** \u2014 reference ppl for all deltas.\n2. **\u03b1=1.0 round-off-only check (C7)** \u2014 no clipping by construction; measured activation MSE should sit near the analytical uniform-source round-off level (SQNR \u2248 6.02N+1.76 dB \u21d2 \u224849.9 dB at 8 bit, \u224825.8 dB at 4 bit for uniform sources; real tensors will differ \u2014 used only as an order-of-magnitude sanity check that the quantizer is implemented correctly, not as a pass/fail oracle).\n3. **Deterministic evaluation** \u2014 fixed segment order, fixed model precision (fp16, single precision policy), fixed thread count, no sampling; one run per config justified by determinism (repeat at \u03b1\\* if nondeterminism detected).\n4. **Trivial-quantization / direction control (C8, \u03b1=0.30)** \u2014 deliberately severe over-clipping; the harness must show ppl(0.30) \u226b ppl(1.0) and a clearly ordered degradation relative to the grid. Failure here invalidates any \"clipping doesn't matter\" conclusion (prevents a false outcome (b)).\n\n## 9. Feasibility (analytical only; nothing below is measured)\n\n- **Compute (analytical):** forward pass \u2248 2\u00b7P_fwd \u2248 **13.4 GFLOP/token** for ~6.7B scoring params. Hypothetically assuming 0.5\u20133 TFLOP/s effective CPU throughput on this 224-core host (not benchmarked): \u2248 **37\u2013225 tokens/s**. Main sweep (9 WikiText-2 runs \u00d7 ~119 segs \u00d7 2048 \u2248 2.2 M tokens) \u21d2 \u2248 **3\u201316 h wall-clock**, inside an assumed 24\u201348 h budget; PTB and sensitivity/ablation tiers add \u227225%.\n- **Reduced-token fallback (explicit):** 32 segments/config (~66k tokens) \u21d2 9 runs in \u2248 **0.7\u20134.4 h** under the same hypothetical throughput; use the full split only for the final three grid points {\u03b1\\*-neighborhood} + C0 + C8. PPL sampling error scales ~1/\u221a(N tokens) (analytical; constant not estimated here).\n- **Memory/storage:** fp16 weights \u224813.5 GB \u226a 2 TB RAM; K4-V4 cache is ~4\u00d7 smaller than fp16 \u2014 no constraint. Workspace has ~50 GB free \u21d2 one local checkpoint copy (~13\u201326 GB) must be reused across all runs; quantization hook overhead is a small per-token elementwise cost (activation quantization is per-token O(d), negligible vs. matmuls).\n- **Software prerequisites to install at implementation time (currently absent, network disabled):** torch, transformers, datasets, numpy/wandb-equivalent logger; a ~30-token smoke test before the sweep to validate hook wiring and to replace the hypothetical throughput figure with a measured one.\n\n## 10. Out of scope\n\nWeight quantization; GPU-specific kernels; any empirical claim about the actual optimum \u03b1 (none is claimed or implied here); full factorial over bit-widths/granularity (explicitly capped at \u22643 sensitivity points).\n\n---\n\n**Fixed requirements vs. assumptions, stated separately:**\n- *Fixed (from brief):* LLAMA2-7B; symmetric input-activation path; asymmetric KV-cache path; perplexity metric; single optimal fixed clipping ratio as headline answer.\n- *Assumptions:* A1 clipping definition (\u03b8=\u03b1\u00b7absmax, \u03b1\u22641) and its 7-point grid; A8 / K4-V4 / per-token / group-32-K / per-channel-V as the anchor configuration (probed, not presumed, via \u00a77); WikiText-2 primary, PTB secondary; 2048-token segments, no sliding window; ~24\u201348 h CPU budget with the \u00a79 fallback; weights unquantized; WikiText-2 test size \u22480.24\u20130.25 M tokens to be confirmed at implementation.", "evidence": "Repo/runtime observations (design constraints): /workspace contains only task.json (\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required\"); no GPU (nvidia-smi driver failure); no network (DNS resolution failure); torch/transformers/datasets/numpy absent on Python 3.14.4; nproc=224, ~2 TB RAM, ~50 GB free on workspace volume. Analytical arithmetic verified with python3 (calculation, not measurement): 2\u00b76.68e9 \u2248 13.4 GFLOP/token forward; 0.5\u20133 TFLOP/s hypothetical \u21d2 37\u2013225 tok/s \u21d2 9 runs \u00d7 ~119\u00d72048-token segments \u2248 2.2M tokens in \u22483\u201316 h (full) or \u22480.7\u20134.4 h at 32-seg fallback; reciprocal grid mapping \u03b2=1/\u03b1 for the multiplier variant = {1.43,1.33,1.25,1.18,1.11,1.05,1.0}; uniform-source SQNR 6.02N+1.76 dB \u21d2 49.9 dB (8-bit), 25.8 dB (4-bit) used only as order-of-magnitude quantizer-sanity check. All 7 researcher binding clarifications incorporated: A1 named as assumption with definition-mapping note (\u00b62); shared \u03b1 primary with 3\u00d73 subgrid demoted to optional tier (\u00b65-A); bit-widths/granularity presented as probeable design parameters with \u22643 sensitivity points, not factorial (\u00b67); fixed requirements stated verbatim with symmetric-input/asymmetric-KV unambiguous throughout (\u00b61); three-way outcome interpretation with explicit falsification patterns (\u00b66); four controls incl. \u03b1=0.30 direction check (\u00b68); feasibility fully analytical with no measured labels and explicit reduced-token budget (\u00b69).", "assumptions": ["A1: clipping ratio defined as \u03b8 = \u03b1\u00b7absmax(unit), \u03b1\u22641, swept over {0.70,0.75,0.80,0.85,0.90,0.95,1.00}; headline answer anchored to this definition, with percentile and >1-multiplier remappings provided", "Anchor configuration A8 per-token symmetric activations; K4-V4 asymmetric KV with K per-token-group(32) / V per-channel \u2014 treated as probeable design parameters (\u22643 sensitivity points), not brief-fixed requirements", "One shared \u03b1 for input and KV paths is the primary result; independent per-path ratios only in the optional 3\u00d73 ablation tier", "WikiText-2 test (~0.24\u20130.25M tokens, to verify) as primary perplexity corpus, 2048-token contiguous segments, no sliding window; PTB as secondary robustness corpus", "Compute budget ~24\u201348 h wall-clock on this 224-core CPU-only host; throughput figures are hypothetical analytical ranges pending a real smoke test; weights remain fp16; design-only \u2014 no experiment executed, no results claimed"], "uncertainties": ["The source paper's actual clipping-ratio definition and grid (topics setup_1/setup_10/setup_17 may pin these; the design's definition-mapping note absorbs percentile or >1-multiplier variants without changing the protocol)", "True bit-width/granularity choices prescribed by the source, if any \u2014 the design treats ours as an anchor and tests shift sensitivity rather than assuming correctness", "Actual CPU throughput for fp16 7B forward passes; the 3\u201316 h full-sweep window rests on an unmeasured 0.5\u20133 TFLOP/s assumption, mitigated by the explicit 32-segment reduced-token fallback", "Exact WikiText-2 test token count after Llama-2 tokenization (affects only segment count and run-time arithmetic, not the protocol)"]}", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
